<title>RUSSIA: Russia to change pension payment system - Yeltsin.</title>
<headline>Russia to change pension payment system - Yeltsin.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia must introduce a pension payment system based on individuals' savings to supplement the current government-backed system, President Boris Yeltsin said in his annual written address to parliament.</p>
<p>&quot;We must gradually augment the current pension system at the expense of individual's savings,&quot; Yeltsin said in the address, an advance copy of which was obtained by Reuters on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He suggested the focus in pension payments could be shifted to individuals' savings.</p>
<p>But introduction of the new system would take no less then 20 years, he said.</p>
<p>Yeltsin ordered the government to prepare a pension reform programme by November 1 and present laws covering it to the Federation Council upper house of parliament by December 1.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
